## Phase 3: Exam Interface
**Duration:** 8 working days (Week 4–5)
**Goal:** The "pressure-cooker" — dual-timer, server-authoritative, non-reversible exam experience.

### Backend Tasks

| # | Task | Days |
|---|---|---|
| 3.1 | `POST /api/session/[id]/start` — write `global_end` and first `q_end` to Redis; update session `status = 'active'`, `started_at` | 1 |
| 3.2 | `POST /api/session/[id]/answer` — validate exam session token, record answer, advance to next question, reset `q_end` in Redis | 1.5 |
| 3.3 | Redis keyspace notifications: `q_end` expiry → auto-advance (log null answer, push next question); `global_end` expiry → auto-submit | 1.5 |
| 3.4 | `POST /api/session/[id]/heartbeat` — return `{ global_remaining_ms, q_remaining_ms, current_q_index, tab_violations }`; accept `{ is_visible, tab_violation }` payload | 1 |
| 3.5 | Tab violation counter: increment on server at violation 1, 2; trigger auto-submit at violation 3 | 0.5 |
| 3.6 | Session reconstruction: if Redis keys missing on heartbeat, reconstruct from `exam_sessions.started_at` + `expires_at` | 0.5 |

### Frontend Tasks

| # | Task | Days |
|---|---|---|
| 3.7 | Global countdown timer component (server-synced, never trusts client clock) | 0.5 |
| 3.8 | Per-question countdown ring/bar (resets on each advance) | 0.5 |
| 3.9 | Question card component: stem, 4 option buttons, immediate lock on selection | 0.5 |
| 3.10 | Heartbeat service (5-second interval) with re-sync on reconnect | 0.5 |
| 3.11 | Tab visibility monitoring (`visibilitychange` + `blur` events), violation toast warnings | 0.5 |
| 3.12 | Anti-cheat: right-click disable, copy-paste disable, dev tools size heuristic flag | 0.5 |
| 3.13 | Network loss banner ("Connection lost — timers continue on server") | 0.25 |
| 3.14 | Auto-redirect to `/results/[id]` on exam completion (heartbeat trigger or WebSocket push) | 0.25 |

### Exit Criteria
- [ ] 15s question timeout fires server-side and auto-advances without client action.
- [ ] 600s global timer submits exam automatically, no client dependency.
- [ ] 3rd tab violation triggers submission.
- [ ] Disconnecting from network for 60s and reconnecting: exam state correctly restored from Redis.
- [ ] Answers are server-locked; cannot be resubmitted once sent.

